This paper examines a subcritical approximation of a critical boundary value problem on a half sphere, specifically:

$$
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
-\Delta u = Q(u) & \mbox{in } \mathbb{S}^n_+ \\
u = 0 & \mbox{on } \partial \mathbb{S}^n_+
\end{array}
\right.
$$

where $\mathbb{S}^n_+$ represents the upper half of the n-dimensional sphere and $Q(u)$ is a function that depends on $u$. By introducing a parameter $\varepsilon$, the authors consider the problem:

$$
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
-\Delta u = \lambda u + \mu Q(u) & \mbox{in } \mathbb{S}^n_+ \\
u = 0 & \mbox{on } \partial \mathbb{S}^n_+
\end{array}
\right.
$$

